% ============================================================================
% ADJ52 case-25 derived rulebook.
% Clinical area: non-resolving focal lung consolidation in an occupationally
% exposed heavy smoker (occupational/inhalational pulmonology).
%
% The diagnostic puzzle the IR poses (q1-q4): a presumed community-acquired
% pneumonia (RIGHT UPPER LOBE air-space consolidation) that FAILED a full
% ~3-week course of IV broad-spectrum antibiotics; a 63yo man, 45 pack-years,
% who arc-welds IRON AND STEEL in a poorly ventilated bay; BAL returns
% ALVEOLAR-MACROPHAGE-PREDOMINANT fluid with only scant neutrophils,
% lymphocytes, and eosinophils; transthoracic biopsy shows NO malignant cells
% and NO vasculitis; serum ANCA negative. CT shows the segmental consolidation
% PLUS small ill-defined nodules PLUS background centrilobular emphysema.
%
% Magnitudes are encoded QUALITATIVELY per adj-lang grammar (lowercase only, no
% leading digits, no uppercase). E.g. smoking_burden(heavy), pao2(mildly_low).
%
% Anti-overfit note: every clause is added because a CITED source supports the
% DIRECTION of the likelihood ratio for that finding in that disease, never to
% steer the case onto a chosen answer. Discriminators that fire NEGATIVE against
% the tempting wrong answers (lung cancer, organizing pneumonia, eosinophilic
% pneumonia, TB, ANCA vasculitis) are included with LR<1 wherever a source
% supports them.
% ============================================================================

% ===== PRIORS (base rates among non-resolving-consolidation referrals) =====

% rationale: A non-resolving pneumonia is a recognized first presentation of
% lung malignancy, and a 63yo with 45 pack-years is high-risk; high prior so the
% engine must EARN the move away from cancer on the negative-biopsy data.
prior 0.28 for diagnosis(lung_adenocarcinoma)
  source "Insights Imaging 2022 13:244 (pneumonic-type lung adenocarcinoma mimics pneumonia); PMC4543828 ('Non-resolving' pneumonia, malignancy first manifestation)" trust authoritative

% rationale: Organizing pneumonia is the prototypical cause of focal/migratory
% air-space consolidation that fails empiric antibiotics for presumed bacterial
% pneumonia; high prior as the leading non-infectious mimic.
prior 0.25 for diagnosis(organizing_pneumonia)
  source "StatPearls NBK507874 (Cryptogenic Organizing Pneumonia); WJGNet 2024 v12 i36 (secondary OP, consolidation unresponsive to antibiotics)" trust authoritative

% rationale: Pulmonary siderosis (welder's lung) is uncommon and classically
% nodular, BUT it is documented to present as air-space CONSOLIDATION mimicking
% pneumonia in an iron arc-welder; lower prior, must be EARNED by the exposure
% and macrophage-predominant BAL.
prior 0.15 for diagnosis(pulmonary_siderosis)
  source "Mukae et al. Respir Med Case Rep 2018, PMC6039750 (pulmonary siderosis misdiagnosed as pneumonia: RUL consolidation, iron welding)" trust authoritative

% rationale: TB favors posterior/apical upper-lobe segments and resolves slowly
% despite antibiotics; a real differential for non-resolving RUL consolidation.
prior 0.12 for diagnosis(pulmonary_tuberculosis)
  source "Radiology Assistant TB imaging (apical/posterior upper-lobe ~85%); PMC4543828 (non-resolving pneumonia DDx includes TB)" trust authoritative

% rationale: Chronic eosinophilic pneumonia gives peripheral upper-zone
% consolidation that fails antibiotics; on the differential of non-resolving
% peripheral air-space disease.
prior 0.10 for diagnosis(chronic_eosinophilic_pneumonia)
  source "Frontiers Med 2024 10.3389/fmed.2024.1355247 (chronic eosinophilic pneumonia, peripheral consolidation)" trust authoritative

% rationale: ANCA-associated vasculitis (GPA) can present with non-resolving
% nodular/consolidative lung disease; included because vasculitis was actively
% excluded in the workup.
prior 0.06 for diagnosis(anca_vasculitis)
  source "Insights Imaging / StatPearls (GPA pulmonary nodules and consolidation in DDx of non-resolving lung opacity)" trust authoritative

% ===== SHARED 'FAILED-ANTIBIOTICS NON-INFECTIVE CONSOLIDATION' SIGNATURE =====
% rationale: 'segmental air-space consolidation that did NOT settle after a full
% broad-spectrum IV course, in an afebrile, well-appearing, normally-saturating
% patient' is ONE correlated gestalt that points away from ordinary bacterial CAP
% and toward a non-infective / occupational cause. It is fired ONCE per non-
% infective conclusion rather than summing the correlated facts (anti-saturation).
% mechanism non_infective_consolidation_gestalt for diagnosis(pulmonary_siderosis) lr 2.2 : consolidation_response_to_antibiotics(none), general_appearance(well_afebrile), air_space_consolidation(segmental_right_upper_lobe)
% mechanism non_infective_consolidation_gestalt for diagnosis(organizing_pneumonia) lr 2.4 : consolidation_response_to_antibiotics(none), general_appearance(well_afebrile), air_space_consolidation(segmental_right_upper_lobe)
% mechanism non_infective_consolidation_gestalt for diagnosis(lung_adenocarcinoma) lr 2.2 : consolidation_response_to_antibiotics(none), general_appearance(well_afebrile), air_space_consolidation(segmental_right_upper_lobe)
% mechanism non_infective_consolidation_gestalt for diagnosis(chronic_eosinophilic_pneumonia) lr 1.8 : consolidation_response_to_antibiotics(none), general_appearance(well_afebrile), air_space_consolidation(segmental_right_upper_lobe)

% ===== PULMONARY SIDEROSIS (welder's lung) =====

% rationale: KEY DISCRIMINATOR — the central, near-specific clue. Daily arc-
% welding of IRON AND STEEL in a poorly ventilated bay is the exposure that
% causes inhaled iron-oxide accumulation in alveolar macrophages (siderosis).
contributes 7.0 from occupational_exposure(iron_steel_arc_welding) to diagnosis(pulmonary_siderosis)
  source "Mukae et al. PMC6039750 (iron arc-welding -> pulmonary siderosis); PubMed 8257971 (occupational siderosis and welders' lung review)" trust authoritative

% rationale: KEY DISCRIMINATOR — poor ventilation / high-dose biopersistent iron
% fume is the dose factor that drives iron-laden-macrophage accumulation and even
% fibrosis; the IR explicitly notes a poorly ventilated bay.
contributes 2.5 from exposure_condition(poorly_ventilated) to diagnosis(pulmonary_siderosis)
  source "RadioGraphics 2001 g01nv011371 (high-dose welding fume + inadequate ventilation in welders' pneumoconiosis)" trust authoritative

% rationale: KEY DISCRIMINATOR — BAL with a MARKED PREDOMINANCE of alveolar
% macrophages (and scant other cells) is exactly the siderosis BAL: iron is
% phagocytosed and accumulates within macrophages (siderophages).
contributes 4.0 from bal_pattern(alveolar_macrophage_predominant) to diagnosis(pulmonary_siderosis)
  source "Mukae et al. PMC6039750 (BAL: many alveolar macrophages containing iron particles); EPA Perls' Prussian blue review (only macrophages stain -> siderophages)" trust authoritative

% rationale: small ILL-DEFINED nodules on CT are the classic siderosis substrate
% (iron-laden macrophages aggregated along peribronchovascular lymphatics);
% co-occurring with the consolidation, they support iron deposition.
contributes 2.2 from ct_pattern(small_ill_defined_nodules) to diagnosis(pulmonary_siderosis)
  source "Clinical Imaging 2023 S0899-7071(23)00034-7 (welders: poorly-defined small centrilobular nodules = radiopaque iron in macrophages)" trust authoritative

% rationale: documented as an air-space CONSOLIDATION presentation of siderosis
% (the very pattern here), so the RUL segmental consolidation is compatible, not
% against, once the exposure is present.
contributes 1.8 from air_space_consolidation(segmental_right_upper_lobe) to diagnosis(pulmonary_siderosis)
  source "Mukae et al. PMC6039750 (first reported siderosis presenting as RUL air-space consolidation rather than nodules)" trust authoritative

% rationale: a clear chest film three months earlier and a sub-acute (~6 week)
% course tracking the recent several months of welding fits an acquired
% inhalational deposition rather than a chronic structural disease.
contributes 1.5 from prior_film(recent_clear) to diagnosis(pulmonary_siderosis)
  source "Mukae et al. PMC6039750 (siderosis develops over months of iron-welding exposure; reversible/accumulative)" trust authoritative

% rationale: KEY SYNERGY — iron-steel welding exposure TOGETHER WITH a macrophage-
% predominant BAL is near-specific for iron-laden-macrophage accumulation; the two
% together carry more than the product of their separate weak signals.
interacts 3.0 when occupational_exposure(iron_steel_arc_welding) and bal_pattern(alveolar_macrophage_predominant) for diagnosis(pulmonary_siderosis)
  source "EPA Perls' Prussian blue review (inhaled biopersistent iron particles phagocytosed by alveolar macrophages -> siderophages on BAL)" trust authoritative

% ===== ORGANIZING PNEUMONIA (leading non-infective mimic — argued down on BAL) =====

% rationale: OP is the classic cause of consolidation that fails empiric
% antibiotics for presumed bacterial pneumonia.
contributes 2.5 from consolidation_response_to_antibiotics(none) to diagnosis(organizing_pneumonia)
  source "WJGNet 2024 v12 i36 6877 (secondary OP: consolidation unresponsive to antibiotics); StatPearls NBK507874" trust authoritative

% rationale: a peribronchial / peripheral segmental air-space consolidation is a
% typical OP distribution (subpleural / peribronchovascular).
contributes 2.0 from air_space_consolidation(segmental_right_upper_lobe) to diagnosis(organizing_pneumonia)
  source "PMC4332061 (COP: airspace consolidation, peribronchovascular/peripheral); ScienceDirect Organizing Pneumonia overview" trust authoritative

% rationale: KEY DISCRIMINATOR (fires NEGATIVE) — OP BAL is characteristically
% LYMPHOCYTE-rich (mixed pattern, lymphocytes ~30-40%). A BAL with a MARKED
% MACROPHAGE predominance and only SCANT lymphocytes argues against OP.
contributes 0.30 from bal_pattern(alveolar_macrophage_predominant) to diagnosis(organizing_pneumonia)
  source "PMC4332061 (migratory/COP BAL macrophages ~51%, lymphocytes ~33%); StatPearls NBK507874 (COP BAL lymphocytosis)" trust authoritative

% rationale: DISCRIMINATOR (fires NEGATIVE, weak) — OP is a histologic diagnosis
% (intra-alveolar fibroblastic/Masson bodies). A needle biopsy of the consolidated
% area that shows NO such organizing features (only non-specific tissue) does not
% support OP; treated as mildly against given the negative histology offered.
contributes 0.6 from biopsy(no_specific_diagnostic_feature) to diagnosis(organizing_pneumonia)
  source "StatPearls NBK507874 (COP diagnosis requires intra-alveolar organizing connective tissue on biopsy)" trust authoritative

% ===== LUNG ADENOCARCINOMA (the high-prior cancer mimic — argued down on biopsy) =====

% rationale: heavy smoking (45 pack-years) is the dominant risk factor for lung
% carcinoma and is why cancer leads the differential of non-resolving
% consolidation in this man.
contributes 2.2 from smoking_burden(heavy_pack_years) to diagnosis(lung_adenocarcinoma)
  source "Insights Imaging 2022 13:244 (smoking-related risk; pneumonic-type adenocarcinoma DDx)" trust authoritative

% rationale: pneumonic-type (mucinous lepidic) adenocarcinoma is the form that
% presents as a consolidation indistinguishable from pneumonia and fails to clear.
contributes 2.0 from air_space_consolidation(segmental_right_upper_lobe) to diagnosis(lung_adenocarcinoma)
  source "PMC3587910 (bronchioloalveolar carcinoma as non-resolving consolidation); Insights Imaging 2022 13:244" trust authoritative

% rationale: KEY DISCRIMINATOR (fires NEGATIVE) — a CT-guided transthoracic needle
% biopsy of the consolidated area showing NO MALIGNANT CELLS substantially lowers
% (but does not exclude) cancer. This is the clause that demotes the tempting
% high-prior cancer label.
contributes 0.20 from biopsy(no_malignant_cells) to diagnosis(lung_adenocarcinoma)
  source "JCDR 60149 (transthoracic biopsy to diagnose pneumonic adenocarcinoma; negative tissue argues against malignancy)" trust authoritative

% rationale: DISCRIMINATOR (fires NEGATIVE) — direct bronchoscopic inspection
% showing NO endobronchial lesion, mass, or obstruction argues against a central
% obstructing tumor causing post-obstructive non-resolution.
contributes 0.5 from bronchoscopy(no_endobronchial_lesion) to diagnosis(lung_adenocarcinoma)
  source "PMC4543828 ('Non-resolving' pneumonia: bronchoscopy to exclude endobronchial obstructing lesion/tumour)" trust authoritative

% ===== PULMONARY TUBERCULOSIS (argued down on clean bronchoscopy / no TB features) =====

% rationale: TB favors the POSTERIOR segment of the upper lobe and resolves
% slowly despite antibacterials — compatible with the RUL posterior-segment site.
contributes 2.0 from air_space_consolidation(segmental_right_upper_lobe) to diagnosis(pulmonary_tuberculosis)
  source "Radiology Assistant TB imaging (posterior/apical upper-lobe ~85%); PMC8743064 (active pulmonary TB)" trust authoritative

% rationale: DISCRIMINATOR (fires NEGATIVE) — an afebrile, well-appearing patient
% with normal saturations and only mild inflammatory markers is atypical for the
% systemic constitutional picture of active pulmonary TB.
contributes 0.5 from general_appearance(well_afebrile) to diagnosis(pulmonary_tuberculosis)
  source "EMCrit IBCC Tuberculosis (constitutional symptoms, fever, weight loss typical of active TB)" trust authoritative

% rationale: DISCRIMINATOR (fires NEGATIVE) — bronchoscopy with NO endobronchial
% lesion argues against endobronchial TB; the consolidation without cavitation /
% nodal disease is less classic for TB.
contributes 0.6 from bronchoscopy(no_endobronchial_lesion) to diagnosis(pulmonary_tuberculosis)
  source "Radiology Assistant TB (cavitation/tree-in-bud/nodal disease typical); CHEST upper-lobe cavitary DDx" trust authoritative

% ===== CHRONIC EOSINOPHILIC PNEUMONIA (argued down on scant BAL eosinophils) =====

% rationale: CEP gives peripheral upper-zone consolidation that fails antibiotics.
contributes 1.8 from air_space_consolidation(segmental_right_upper_lobe) to diagnosis(chronic_eosinophilic_pneumonia)
  source "Frontiers Med 2024 1355247 (CEP: peripheral consolidation, 'photographic negative of pulmonary edema')" trust authoritative

% rationale: KEY DISCRIMINATOR (fires NEGATIVE) — CEP is DEFINED by BAL
% eosinophilia (>=40%). A BAL with only SCANT eosinophils and macrophage
% predominance is strongly against CEP.
contributes 0.15 from bal_eosinophils(scant) to diagnosis(chronic_eosinophilic_pneumonia)
  source "Frontiers Med 2024 1355247 (CEP requires BAL eosinophils >=40% or blood eosinophilia >=1000)" trust authoritative

% ===== ANCA-ASSOCIATED VASCULITIS / GPA (argued down on negative ANCA + biopsy) =====

% rationale: GPA can cause non-resolving nodules / consolidation, hence it was
% actively investigated here.
contributes 1.5 from ct_pattern(small_ill_defined_nodules) to diagnosis(anca_vasculitis)
  source "StatPearls / RadioGraphics (GPA: pulmonary nodules and consolidation)" trust authoritative

% rationale: KEY DISCRIMINATOR (fires NEGATIVE) — a NEGATIVE serum ANCA panel
% lowers the probability of ANCA-associated vasculitis.
contributes 0.30 from serology(anca_negative) to diagnosis(anca_vasculitis)
  source "StatPearls (ANCA sensitivity in active GPA; negative ANCA lowers pretest probability)" trust authoritative

% rationale: KEY DISCRIMINATOR (fires NEGATIVE) — a biopsy of the lesion showing
% NO features of vasculitis argues against pulmonary vasculitis.
contributes 0.30 from biopsy(no_vasculitis) to diagnosis(anca_vasculitis)
  source "StatPearls (GPA histology: necrotizing granulomatous vasculitis; absence argues against)" trust authoritative

% ===== NEXT STEP (confirmatory pathway) =====

% rationale: the decisive next step is a PERLS' PRUSSIAN BLUE (iron) STAIN of the
% BAL fluid and/or the biopsy specimen: iron-laden macrophages (siderophages)
% staining strongly positive confirm siderosis and, with malignancy/TB/vasculitis
% excluded, close the case. Highest value-of-information step.
prior 0.25 for next_step(prussian_blue_iron_stain_of_bal_and_biopsy)
  source "Mukae et al. PMC6039750 (Prussian blue-positive iron-laden macrophages confirmed siderosis); EPA Perls' review" trust authoritative
contributes 5.0 from bal_pattern(alveolar_macrophage_predominant) to next_step(prussian_blue_iron_stain_of_bal_and_biopsy)
  source "EPA Perls' Prussian blue review (macrophage-predominant BAL -> stain for iron to identify siderophages)" trust authoritative
contributes 4.0 from occupational_exposure(iron_steel_arc_welding) to next_step(prussian_blue_iron_stain_of_bal_and_biopsy)
  source "Mukae et al. PMC6039750 (iron-welding history -> pursue iron staining of BAL/tissue)" trust authoritative
contributes 2.0 from biopsy(no_malignant_cells) to next_step(prussian_blue_iron_stain_of_bal_and_biopsy)
  source "Mukae et al. PMC6039750 (malignancy excluded on tissue -> apply Prussian blue to confirm iron deposition)" trust authoritative

% rationale: an alternative confirmatory arm is a surgical / larger tissue lung
% biopsy if histology remains non-diagnostic; lower prior than the simple stain.
prior 0.12 for next_step(surgical_lung_biopsy)
  source "PMC4543828 ('Non-resolving' pneumonia: surgical lung biopsy when less invasive sampling non-diagnostic)" trust authoritative
contributes 1.5 from biopsy(no_specific_diagnostic_feature) to next_step(surgical_lung_biopsy)
  source "PMC4543828 (proceed to surgical lung biopsy after non-diagnostic needle biopsy)" trust authoritative

% ===== UNCERTAINTIES (decision-relevant, unresolved) =====

% u-iron-stain: the Perls' Prussian blue result on the BAL/biopsy is NOT yet
% reported; it is the single highest-value discriminator. A strongly positive
% iron stain is near-dispositive for siderosis; a negative stain argues strongly
% against and reopens the non-iron differential.
contributes 12.0 from iron_stain(strongly_positive_siderophages) to diagnosis(pulmonary_siderosis)
  source "Mukae et al. PMC6039750 (markedly Prussian blue-positive iron-laden macrophages confirm siderosis)" trust authoritative
contributes 0.12 from iron_stain(negative) to diagnosis(pulmonary_siderosis)
  source "EPA Perls' review (absence of stainable iron in macrophages argues against siderosis)" trust authoritative
uncertain { iron_stain(strongly_positive_siderophages), iron_stain(negative) } for diagnosis(pulmonary_siderosis)
  source "Mukae et al. PMC6039750 (Prussian blue iron stain not yet performed; decisive confirmatory discriminator)"
